# Disk, floppy and tape images live in diskimages/ and are kept in the
# repository in compressed form only: demo expands "<image>.gz" by itself when
# the image it is told to mount cannot be opened (10.02_devices/2_src/
# storageimage.cpp). The uncompressed copy is a product of a run, and is
# ignored here so it cannot be committed by accident. The ".gz" stays tracked.
#
# Every image carries a ".dsk" extension, the medium in front of it
# (rt11v5.5.rl02.dsk.gz, v6bin.rk05.dsk.gz, RTRKV4.00.rk05.dsk.gz), so one
# pattern covers them all - and the pattern cannot collide with the example
# directories, which are named after the medium too (rt11.rl02/, unixv6.rk05/).
# A pattern matches a directory as readily as a file, and an excluded directory
# takes everything below it with it.

*.dsk

# One compressed master is excluded as well: 300 MB, over the 100 MB limit
# GitHub enforces on a single file, and it does not compress further. It is the
# DECUS data disk on uda1 of the RSX11M-PLUS example, not the disk that example
# boots from. See diskimages/rsx11mpv4.6_du1_84.ra80.dsk.gz.txt.
diskimages/rsx11mpv4.6_du1_84.ra80.dsk.gz

# Not ignored, and not images: the papertape and absolute-loader programs
# (*.ptap, *.abs), the MACRO-11 sources and listings (*.mac, *.lst), the SimH
# configurations (*.simh*, *.ini) and the reference URLs - all small and all
# kept uncompressed.
